 The classification performance is evaluated using confusion matrix. Figure  13 a, b, and c illustrates the confusion matrix for humidity (LR, DT and RF) classification respectively, showing correctly and incorrectly predicted humidity levels. The diagonal values indicate accurate classifications, while off-diagonal values represent misclassifications. This graphic helps in evaluating model performance through the use of metrics such as F1-score, recall, accuracy, and precision 55 . 
